  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 'What is the G Protein''s primary role in the cell?



'
    basic: G protein relays external signals to the cell interior.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: The G protein activation cycle acts like a molecular switch that controls
      the identity and potency of various cellular processes.
  - title: 'What does G Protein do in this nexus?



'
    basic: "The G protein binds to GLP-1R. This activates the G protein complex,
      causing it to split into subunits. \nThe activated subunit of G protein (G
      alpha) then carries a signal from GLP-1R away to another protein."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "G protein complex binds to the binding pocket at the intracellular
      domain of GLP-1R. \nIt separates into G alpha and G beta- gamma dimer upon
      exchanging GDP to GTP. \nThe active G alpha subunit activates AC in the next
      step, continuing the insulin secretion pathway."
